(Postmortem INC-7373: inventory-api upstream rate limiting \(HTTP 429\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Date: April 2026. Duration: 34 minutes. Severity: SEV2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Summary) Tj T*
(Customers saw errors from inventory-api for 34 minutes. The trigger was upstream rate limiting) Tj T*
(\(HTTP 429\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Timeline) Tj T*
(09:12 alert fired. 09:20 incident declared. 09:49 mitigation applied.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Root cause) Tj T*
(A change merged two days earlier removed a safety limit, so upstream rate limiting \(HTTP 429\)) Tj T*
(was able to build up unnoticed until peak traffic. Monitoring did not alert early because the) Tj T*
(threshold was set for the old traffic pattern.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Contributing factors) Tj T*
(- The runbook pointed to a dashboard that had been renamed.) Tj T*
(- The canary stage was skipped for a config-only change.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Action items) Tj T*
(- AI-818: restore the safety limit and add a regression test.) Tj T*
(- AI-799: update the alert threshold to the new traffic pattern.) Tj T*
(- AI-763: never skip the canary, including for config changes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
